    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0220" n="954" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg954"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Baron
                            Fava.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 88.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have a confidential communication,
                    under date of October 29, from the governor of Colorado, respecting the
                    postponement of the criminal proceedings against the Walsenburg Italian
                    lynchers, the substance of which I shall be glad to make known to you at our
                    next interview.</p>
                <p>The governor expresses the strongest desire that the guilty parties may be
                    punished and his conviction that the postponement is a necessary means to that
                    end.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
